00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:22.120
The rest of the analysis remains as I made
it earlier this week.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:28.670
Today, the house of representatives is expected
to formally vote to impeach president Donald

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:29.670
Trump.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.600
Uh, it may carry over until tomorrow.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.750
Republican starting off the hearings this
morning with a number of attempts to delay,

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.020
uh, various obstructive attempts, including
one where they opened up and said, Hey, we

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.839
actually just moved to adjourn.

00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:43.390
Let's just cancel it all and go home.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:48.340
Of course, a move, uh, that Democrats who
have the majority in the house, uh, voted

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.600
down right away.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.070
Depending on how long debate goes today.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:56.030
By the time that you listen to today's show,
watch today's show, Donald Trump may already

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:00.069
be impeached or they may not have voted and
maybe that vote will be forthcoming tomorrow

00:01:00.069 --> 00:01:02.100
or in the following days.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:08.210
Yesterday rallies exploding across the country
in support of Donald Trump's pea impeachment.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.759
Now, I wasn't sure how much attendance these
rallies would see, but it was truly stunning.

00:01:13.759 --> 00:01:21.080
Huge crowds in major cities and moderately
sized cities and towns all across the United

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.080
States.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:27.380
A very large turnout in New York city, just
one of roughly 600 events, people gathering

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.750
in times square.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:34.380
Many protests here in Massachusetts, including
in Boston as well as in Cambridge.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:40.380
Huge crowds in different parts of Michigan,
Nashville, Tennessee, Washington state.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:45.540
I could not possibly list all of the places
because it was all over the country in both

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.689
blue States and red States.

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:52.320
I heard from people in Oklahoma who said that
they were at impeachment rallies.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:58.039
People seemingly ready for when Donald Trump
will no longer be a thing in the news anymore.

00:01:58.039 --> 00:02:00.069
And of course that will be a long time.

00:02:00.069 --> 00:02:02.929
Uh, this is just the very, very beginning.

00:02:02.929 --> 00:02:05.350
So the house of representatives may have already
voted.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:06.350
We'll be voting today.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:11.000
We'll be voting soon, six hours of debate
scheduled on the issue.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.890
We don't know whether this is going to extend
beyond today.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:21.120
Uh, but we are going to see only the third
ever impeachment of a president of the United

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.120
States.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:25.350
Of course, Andrew Johnson being impeached,
but acquitted.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:28.580
Bill Clinton impeached also acquitted.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:34.110
And a lot of folks incorrectly believe that,
um, Richard Nixon was impeached.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:39.530
Remember Richard Nixon resigned after it became
clear because Republican senators went to

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:42.820
him and said, listen, you've lost the support
of the public.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.090
Even Republican voters don't support you.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:49.000
If impeachment happens, we will have to convict
you.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.860
And that pushed Richard Nixon to resign.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:57.380
Uh, that is, um, a very different scenario
than what we have today.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:02.860
In great part because Richard Nixon didn't
have the benefit of the 24, seven conservative

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:08.250
media cycle, social media, micro-targeting
on all of these different platforms, which

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:13.280
have made it so that 62% of Trump has say,
I don't care what Trump does.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:18.070
He can't even hypothetically do anything that
would get me to reconsider my support for

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.070
him.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:24.860
So let me remind everyone that the Trumpist
right is pretending that what we are seeing

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.860
right now is mere partisanship.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:32.530
But remember the nationwide rallies calling
for the impeachment of Barack Obama.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:37.720
I don't remember them because they didn't
happen and Obama did some bad things for sure.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.140
Remember the nationwide rallies calling for
the impeachment of George W. Bush?

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:42.140
No.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:46.570
As the run any Bush did terrible things and
people did rally correctly against the Iraq

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:47.570
war.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:48.840
But this is not normal.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.160
Not every president generates impeachment.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.950
Again, only three have Donald Trump being
the third.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:59.730
And not every president catalyzes nationwide
rallies demanding that they be impeached.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:04.420
Donald Trump tweeting this morning more than
20 times by the time that the impeachment

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:10.100
debate, uh, started in the house, clearly
bracing for it today, including saying, quote,

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:15.720
can you believe that I will be impeached today
by the radical left, do nothing.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:18.829
Democrats and I did nothing wrong.

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:24.690
Exclamation point, a terrible thing with a
capital T. read the transcripts with attack

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:25.690
capital to you.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:29.540
Of course he has not released the transcripts
from the Ukraine phone call releasing only

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.960
a fraction of it.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:36.530
This should never happen to another president
again saying, say a prayer, Trump calling

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:38.050
for prayer, religious.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:44.360
All of a sudden now that he is getting impeached,
so this is all historic.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:47.010
We are covering it all still.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:51.850
The most likely outcome is that Donald Trump
would be acquitted by the Senate impeachment

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:57.510
trial, but I want to take this as an opportunity
because we are seeing rallies around the country

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:05.230
to remind folks that we need to see crowds
and rallies just as big and bigger nationally

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:12.350
fighting for the climate, fighting to take
back control of our country from the corporate

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:19.460
lobbyist revolving door industrial complex
that we see, the financialization of the economy

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.820
that we've talked about.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:25.310
I've talked before many times about how what
we really need, you know, signing petitions

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:29.590
is not going to achieve change in this country.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:33.970
Calling our elected officials alone is not
going to achieve change in this country.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:37.770
Beyond removing Donald Trump, I'm talking
about the structural problems that we have,

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.430
healthcare, climate inequality, all of these
things.

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:45.210
One of the things I've been talking about
for a long time is we need mass rallies at

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:47.000
urban centers.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:53.470
And the problem is that the system that we
are trying to change by its nature makes it

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:58.639
so that people can't afford to go and do these
mass rallies when people can't miss a day

00:05:58.639 --> 00:05:59.730
of work.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:02.450
Because then that means they don't have the
money for rent.

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:06.730
They're not going to go to their nearest urban
center and mass rally.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:11.540
We need, I've talked about other strategies
that is serious protest strategies, strategic

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:16.520
defaults for example, and all of these other
things that we've discussed many times crippling

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:21.870
industry to the degree that it makes our government
have to fix some of the problems.

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:26.210
Um, we need to see that kind of activism around
more than just impeaching Donald Trump.

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:31.000
I hope this will, the 600 rallies yesterday
will serve as a reminder that people can get

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.650
organized to that degree.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:37.580
Uh, but there are going to be some pains in
it because the system is designed to keep

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:42.510
people in an economically precarious state
such that they can't afford to take a day

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:43.510
off.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:44.510
And to go and do this stuff.

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:46.120
So, uh, that's the way the system works.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.870
I, I'm inspired by the rallies we saw yesterday.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:51.889
We will see the impeachment of Donald Trump
and likely the acquittal.

00:06:51.889 --> 00:06:57.150
But let's remember that the mass rallies in
urban centers should be utilized as a tool

00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:55.310
far beyond simply saying, we want Trump

00:07:55.310 --> 00:08:12.880
to go.

